        "a": "A little, but usually less than you'd expect. Two live webpages use more memory than one, the same way two browser tabs use more than a single tab does, but the difference between that and a single window is small on any computer bought in the last several years. What actually slows a machine down is a page that's heavy on its own, autoplaying video or a chat app refreshing nonstop, far more than the raw number of sites on screen. If one of your sites is like that, put it to sleep or close it when you're not using it, and everything else stays just as responsive."
